<title>FRANCE: Gascogne 96 sales slip but sees profit up.</title>
<headline>Gascogne 96 sales slip but sees profit up.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					 2,895    vs    3,027</p>
<p>NOTE - Wood, pulp and paper producer Gascogne, based in the south-western French town of Dax, said in a statement that good margins and productivity meant it would meet its forecast of a significant rise in profit, before exceptionals, despite the drop of 4.3 percent in total consolidated sales.</p>
<p>Sales abroad were stable at 820 million francs versus 817 in 1995, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
